            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Curiosity | Textbook of Science | Grade 6"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.083,
            0.899,
            0.111,
            0.915
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "56"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.084,
            0.883,
            0.142
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Culinary practices have changed over time. There is a significant difference between traditional and modern methods of cooking food."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.147,
            0.883,
            0.186
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Food provides us energy, support growth, repairs our bodies and protects us from diseases."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.191,
            0.883,
            0.249
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The major nutrients in our food are carbohydrates, fats, proteins, vitamins, and minerals. In addition, food also contains dietary fibres and water."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.254,
            0.882,
            0.294
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Carbohydrates and fats are primary energy sources, while proteins are body-building nutrients."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.298,
            0.882,
            0.338
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Vitamins and minerals strengthen our body, protect us from infections, and keep us healthy."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.342,
            0.883,
            0.382
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " A balanced diet provides all the essential nutrients in the right quantities, along with adequate roughage and water."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.386,
            0.883,
            0.425
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Deficiency of one or more nutrients in our diet for a long time can lead to deficiency diseases and disorders."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.43,
            0.883,
            0.487
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Junk foods are unhealthy as they contain high levels of sugar and fats but little protein, minerals, vitamins, and dietary fibres."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.493,
            0.884,
            0.57
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Millets are known as nutri-cereals as they provide most of the nutrients required for the normal functioning of our bodies. They can be easily cultivated in different climatic conditions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.576,
            0.883,
            0.634
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Eating food that is locally grown and plant-based, to the extent possible, is not only healthy for our bodies but is also good for our environment and our planet."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.638,
            0.883,
            0.697
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The distance travelled by a food item, from the place of its production to the consumer, is called food miles. We must aim to minimise food miles."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.702,
            0.882,
            0.74
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " We should never waste food and only take as much as we can consume."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.316,
            0.778,
            0.721,
            0.802
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us enhance our learning"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
